y is involved, but I wonder if he\u2019s willing to help with two yellows. There\u2019s a possibility to convert Ventnor into Boardwalk, and I'll strategize options for cash to sweeten the deal.**Reassessing trade offers**\n\nI\u2019m considering whether I need to keep Atlantic or not. What if I offer Penn plus cash for Marvin? If I give Penn to Gemini, they'll get a red property they already have. There could be a risk in giving Gemini a yellow monopoly, making it a bad trade for me. Offering Boardwalk seems out of the question now. I might think about offering $500 plus Penn and perhaps GOJF for Marvin, but I\u2019ll need enough cash to status properties before building.**Reevaluating building costs**\n\nIf I pay $500, I'm left with $315, then need to unmortgage properties for $297, which doesn\u2019t leave enough for building. That\u2019s not good. I should consider offering $300 plus Penn and GOJF, which could give me $515 in cash. But even then, unmortgaging and trying to build just one house for $450 seems impossible. I think I can put just one house on a property for $150, but I need to manage my investments carefully!**Considering mortgage options**\n\nI'm thinking about whether I could mortgage one green property, but it seems tricky with the current setup. Only the Baltic has been mortgaged already, so I can't fully mortgage one. Maybe I could build two houses on two properties, which would cost 400, leaving me with 115. If I have nothing on the third property, is that legal? The difference is 1, so maybe I can proceed with that plan.**Assessing Monopoly trade options**\n\nAfter reaching cash of 465, I can buy two greenhouses but might want to hold onto 65 instead. If I accept, I could raise the value to 200, leaving me with 515. I\u2019m considering offers totaling 970 compared to 600 while factoring in mortgage liabilities. Requesting both greenhouses seems good, as we\u2019re keeping Penn but losing some key properties. Plus, there\u2019s some potential